 see this segment hear  this segment and not know me  everything i'm saying here is my best  faith analysis of the situation  and it is with me speaking as an  unfettered defender of trans rights who  understands that this is not a simple  situation and understands the bad faith  nature of why the right keeps saying  give us a definition for woman so ryan  wrote to me  and he explained  david here's why these things are so  tough and meaningless in the abstract  let's say i ask you to define life okay  that's pretty easy right i'll look it up  in the dictionary and let's start with  the dictionary definition why not so a  dictionary definition for life is quote  life  the condition  that distinguishes animals and plants  from inorganic matter  including the capacity for growth  reproduction functional activity and  continual change preceding death  great so now i've bought in  i've picked the definition and that's  what blackburn wanted all the  republicans wanted right  was just pick a definition and give us  that definition but wait a second  are children not life david because they  that was in your definition reproduction  and they can't reproduce  yet  oh that's right that wasn't my  definition what about the elderly who no  longer grow  and who also no longer reproduce oh no  no problem let me tweak the definition  now i've got it i'm gonna get to it okay  the definition is to account for people  who are too young or too old to  reproduce let's have a new a different  definition of life  it's the condition of an organism  that ever had  or will have  that capability of reproduction and  growth then it's life  that's tough that's tough some people  are born without ever having the  capability for reproduction a man with a  sperm disorder kleinfelter syndrome a  woman with certain conditions damn okay  all right well let me walk it back again  so i say  what matters is the species as a whole  if this is a species that as a whole  reproduces even if individual members  for whatever reason might not be able to  then that meets the definition of life  oh no what about mules a mule is what  happens when you breed a female horse  and a male donkey  and they're sterile as a species they  can't reproduce  mules aren't alive now based on my  definition  so you can very quickly see how this  just define it just give us a definition  it's not only bad faith  in theory but it's also really tough in  practice so now let's apply it to the  question of what is a woman  during our interview  michael knowles suggested a few  definitions and one of them check out  the interview if you're interested one  definition he said was it's  anything and anybody that isn't a man  well 1.7 of the population is born  intersexed meaning with both genitals  or with some ambiguity in terms of the  genitalia so if you say if it's if if  they're not a man they're a woman  that definition doesn't account for that  it doesn't work  then nulls said well it's a human that  produces eggs  so a lot of conditions including  hormonal imbalances and thyroid  conditions things in the womb pituitary  tumors that prevent some women from  producing eggs or being able to  reproduce well what about  capability of reproduction through  pregnancy a human with the capability of  reproduction through pregnancy  tons of conditions that inhibit  reproduction and then you've got  post-menopausal women that can't  reproduce but are they not women very  few people would argue that so the point  here is these definitions do not work  for determining  who is a woman since not all biological  women are able to do these things not  all biological women menstruate for  different medical reasons  imagine defining men  simply by their ability to i don't know  impregnate someone or have an erection  so now let's come around to the question  that is actually underlying all of this  for many republicans because  you you have to really understand the  political angle here  they have started