ld do all those  things but  if i sue i'm not going to be able to  show that i was seen as a woman and that  is paramount to proving that you were  discriminated against for gender reasons  now on the other hand if a trans woman  is seen as a woman in whatever situation  they're suing over and they can show  that  why shouldn't they be able to bring such  a lawsuit i mean think about it in many  states you can be fired  for your real or perceived sexual  orientation even if you aren't a gay man  if you're fired because your boss is  homophobic and thought you were gay you  can sue even though you're not actually  a gay man  and similarly  the point here is when they talk about  anybody can just sue and say i was  discriminated against because i'm a  woman well  can you actually show anybody believed  you were a woman in the sense of how  they related to you and their alleged  discrimination so the big point here is  when right wingers ask this stuff number  one it's obviously in bad faith  number two  whatever you say is going to be used  against you but number three  it's actually a lot more complicated  than they pretend these definitions to  be  if we think about it from a legal  standpoint and we talk it through we  actually can make quite a bit of headway  so let me know your thoughts and  hopefully we've touched on what are some  of the  really underlying issues and questions  here uh that that exist  one of our sponsors is blinkist who's  been supporting the david pakman show  longer than any other sponsor blinkist  is the app that lets you listen to or  read an entire non-fiction book in just  15 minutes blinkist is the way to absorb  those books you can't make time for  blinkist takes top non-fiction titles  pulls out the book's key takeaways and  insights and gives it to you in the form  of a text or audio explainer that you  can consume in 15 minutes with blinkist  now you actually do have time to learn  about all the things you've been wanting  to tackle